Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:08:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] downloads: mux videos into the private cache instead of a
 SAF document

ffmpeg-kit writes SAF outputs through its "saf:<id>" pseudo protocol:
Downloader creates "<episode>.tmp" in the SAF download directory, hands
the content URI to ffmpeg-kit and ffmpeg-kit opens it with
ContentResolver.openFileDescriptor() from a native callback. On HarmonyOS
ZhuoyiTong (and on some Motorola/Samsung firmwares, see
aniyomiorg/aniyomi#2126) that open fails with

  Failed to open SAF id: 8 ... IllegalArgumentException: Failed to
  determine if primary:Documents/Anikku/downloads/<...>/Video_tmp/Video.tmp
  is child of primary:Documents/Anikku: FileNotFoundException: Missing file

so every attempt ends with "Error in ffmpeg!" and the episode is retried
forever.

Make ffmpeg write to a plain file in Context.cacheDir
(harmony_download_tmp/<animeId>/<episode>.mkv) instead, then copy the
finished video into the SAF directory as "<episode>.tmp" and rename it to
"<episode>.mkv" with renameToOrCopy(). The copy uses the ordinary
createFile()/openOutputStream() path that image downloads already rely on,
so no SAF feature beyond the ones used elsewhere in the app is required.

- The muxed file survives retries of the copy step so a SAF hiccup does not
  re-download the whole video; a failed ffmpeg run is retried from scratch.
- The cache file is always deleted afterwards, also on cancellation, and
  the private cache is never indexed by gallery apps.
- The external downloader path (1DM/ADM) is unchanged.
